  <h2>“Just enough” wasn’t enough</h2>
  <p>
    It was supposed to be a quick MVP for a job assignment. I got too interested in legal text and kept
    going until it was a product.<Cite id="clausecraft" />
  </p>

  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Generates a complete contract from a prompt or a guided questionnaire.</li>
    <li>Analyses each clause for risk.</li>
    <li>Reviews the whole contract for missing clauses and compliance issues.</li>
    <li>Inline editing with undo and redo, then export.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Decisions</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Privacy first.</strong> No accounts and no server-side storage: drafts live in the browser’s
    localStorage, and only the text being analysed goes to the model.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Model calls behind Edge Functions.</strong> Supabase Edge Functions call the Hugging Face Router,
    so no keys reach the client and models can be swapped. <Todo>which models, and why</Todo>
  </p>

